# Golden frames are compared byte for byte. A CRLF checkout on Windows would fail every
# snapshot test in CI for reasons that have nothing to do with the code (OXD-036).
*.snap text eol=lf

# The PDF fixtures are mostly ASCII, so git's heuristic reads them as text and rewrites their
# line endings on a Windows checkout. Every added byte shifts the cross-reference table, and the
# file stops parsing: `InvalidTrailer`, from a file nobody edited. That is exactly how the
# windows-latest job failed on the OXD-060 pull request (#13).
*.pdf binary
